{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definitions can contain plain React nodes or renderer components for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":". Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so each value is interpreted correctly and receives its typed table context."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the recommended component wrapper. Give it exactly one table object: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":". It then selects the correct column definition and context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  table.getHeaderGroups().map((headerGroup) => (\n    <tr key={headerGroup.id}>\n      {headerGroup.headers.map((header) => (\n        <th key={header.id}>\n          {header.isPlaceholder ? null : <table.FlexRender header={header} />}\n        </th>\n      ))}\n    </tr>\n  ))\n}\n\n{\n  table.getRowModel().rows.map((row) => (\n    <tr key={row.id}>\n      {row.getVisibleCells().map((cell) => (\n        <td key={cell.id}>\n          <table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n        </td>\n      ))}\n    </tr>\n  ))\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter attaches "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" to the table instance, and you can also import it directly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nconst footerContent = <FlexRender footer={header} />","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cells, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" renders "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" when the cell is aggregated, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":" when no aggregated renderer exists, and renders nothing for grouping placeholder cells."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the lower-level function. Use it when you already have a renderable value and its props:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { flexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It distinguishes React components, including class components, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memo"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardRef"},{"type":"text","value":", from already-created React nodes. It does not select "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":" versus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" or suppress grouping placeholders. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" wrapper handles those table-specific decisions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-renderer-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Renderer Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer functions are treated as React components and receive the appropriate context as props:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', {\n    header: ({ column }) => <button>{column.id}</button>,\n    cell: ({ getValue }) => <strong>{getValue()}</strong>,\n  }),\n])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getValue()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.renderValue()"},{"type":"text","value":" when you only need the accessor value. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" when rendering the column definition, because it supports static nodes and component renderers and passes the full context."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Placeholder headers are a layout decision and are not automatically suppressed. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.isPlaceholder"},{"type":"text","value":" unless the placeholder intentionally supplies content for a spanning header. Footer groups contain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Header"},{"type":"text","value":" objects too, so pass each footer header through the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" prop."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","text":"FlexRender vs flexRender","level":2},{"id":"column-renderer-components","text":"Column Renderer Components","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nColumn definitions can contain plain React nodes or renderer components for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so each value is interpreted correctly and receives its typed table context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended component wrapper. Give it exactly one table object: `cell`, `header`, or `footer`. It then selects the correct column definition and context:\n\n```tsx\n{\n  table.getHeaderGroups().map((headerGroup) => (\n    <tr key={headerGroup.id}>\n      {headerGroup.headers.map((header) => (\n        <th key={header.id}>\n          {header.isPlaceholder ? null : <table.FlexRender header={header} />}\n        </th>\n      ))}\n    </tr>\n  ))\n}\n\n{\n  table.getRowModel().rows.map((row) => (\n    <tr key={row.id}>\n      {row.getVisibleCells().map((cell) => (\n        <td key={cell.id}>\n          <table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n        </td>\n      ))}\n    </tr>\n  ))\n}\n```\n\nThe adapter attaches `FlexRender` to the table instance, and you can also import it directly:\n\n```tsx\nimport { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nconst footerContent = <FlexRender footer={header} />\n```\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` renders `aggregatedCell` when the cell is aggregated, falls back to `cell` when no aggregated renderer exists, and renders nothing for grouping placeholder cells.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function. Use it when you already have a renderable value and its props:\n\n```tsx\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt distinguishes React components, including class components, `memo`, and `forwardRef`, from already-created React nodes. It does not select `cell` versus `aggregatedCell` or suppress grouping placeholders. The `FlexRender` wrapper handles those table-specific decisions.\n\n## Column Renderer Components\n\nRenderer functions are treated as React components and receive the appropriate context as props:\n\n```tsx\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', {\n    header: ({ column }) => <button>{column.id}</button>,\n    cell: ({ getValue }) => <strong>{getValue()}</strong>,\n  }),\n])\n```\n\nUse `cell.getValue()` or `cell.renderValue()` when you only need the accessor value. Use `FlexRender` when rendering the column definition, because it supports static nodes and component renderers and passes the full context.\n\nPlaceholder headers are a layout decision and are not automatically suppressed. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless the placeholder intentionally supplies content for a spanning header. Footer groups contain `Header` objects too, so pass each footer header through the `footer` prop.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (React) Guide\n---\n\nColumn definitions can contain plain React nodes or renderer components for `header`, `cell`, `footer`, and `aggregatedCell`. Use TanStack Table's rendering utilities so each value is interpreted correctly and receives its typed table context.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the recommended component wrapper. Give it exactly one table object: `cell`, `header`, or `footer`. It then selects the correct column definition and context:\n\n```tsx\n{\n  table.getHeaderGroups().map((headerGroup) => (\n    <tr key={headerGroup.id}>\n      {headerGroup.headers.map((header) => (\n        <th key={header.id}>\n          {header.isPlaceholder ? null : <table.FlexRender header={header} />}\n        </th>\n      ))}\n    </tr>\n  ))\n}\n\n{\n  table.getRowModel().rows.map((row) => (\n    <tr key={row.id}>\n      {row.getVisibleCells().map((cell) => (\n        <td key={cell.id}>\n          <table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n        </td>\n      ))}\n    </tr>\n  ))\n}\n```\n\nThe adapter attaches `FlexRender` to the table instance, and you can also import it directly:\n\n```tsx\nimport { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nconst footerContent = <FlexRender footer={header} />\n```\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` renders `aggregatedCell` when the cell is aggregated, falls back to `cell` when no aggregated renderer exists, and renders nothing for grouping placeholder cells.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function. Use it when you already have a renderable value and its props:\n\n```tsx\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nflexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt distinguishes React components, including class components, `memo`, and `forwardRef`, from already-created React nodes. It does not select `cell` versus `aggregatedCell` or suppress grouping placeholders. The `FlexRender` wrapper handles those table-specific decisions.\n\n## Column Renderer Components\n\nRenderer functions are treated as React components and receive the appropriate context as props:\n\n```tsx\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', {\n    header: ({ column }) => <button>{column.id}</button>,\n    cell: ({ getValue }) => <strong>{getValue()}</strong>,\n  }),\n])\n```\n\nUse `cell.getValue()` or `cell.renderValue()` when you only need the accessor value. Use `FlexRender` when rendering the column definition, because it supports static nodes and component renderers and passes the full context.\n\nPlaceholder headers are a layout decision and are not automatically suppressed. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless the placeholder intentionally supplies content for a spanning header. Footer groups contain `Header` objects too, so pass each footer header through the `footer` prop.\n"}
